@host = http://localhost:5225

### Health check
GET {{host}}/health

### 1. Register a power meter
POST {{host}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "METER-TEST",
  "mac": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01",
  "location": "FacilityA/Zone1/SubZoneB",
  "category": "PowerConsumption",
  "expectedIntervalMs": 1000
}

### 2. Send a normal reading (expect 202)
POST {{host}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "METER-TEST",
  "timestampUtc": "2026-09-13T14:22:31Z",
  "category": "PowerConsumption",
  "valueKind": "Int",
  "value": 500
}

### 3. Send a reading that crosses the alert band
POST {{host}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "METER-TEST",
  "timestampUtc": "2026-09-13T14:22:32Z",
  "category": "PowerConsumption",
  "valueKind": "Int",
  "value": 1200
}

### 4. Read the retained window back
GET {{host}}/api/telemetry/METER-TEST

### 5. The deployment tree with recursive rollups
GET {{host}}/api/topology

### 6. Every registered sensor
GET {{host}}/api/sensors

### 7. Silence a node, it goes stale within ~3 intervals
POST {{host}}/api/debug/silence/METER-TEST

### 8. Which nodes are currently silenced
GET {{host}}/api/debug/silence

### 9. Restore it
DELETE {{host}}/api/debug/silence/METER-TEST

###
### Rejection cases
###

### Unregistered node (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "GHOST",
  "timestampUtc": "2026-09-13T14:22:31Z",
  "category": "Environmental",
  "valueKind": "Float",
  "value": 42.5
}

### Wrong category for this node (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "METER-TEST",
  "timestampUtc": "2026-09-13T14:22:33Z",
  "category": "Environmental",
  "valueKind": "Float",
  "value": 42.5
}

### Tagged Bool but carries a number (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "METER-TEST",
  "timestampUtc": "2026-09-13T14:22:34Z",
  "category": "PowerConsumption",
  "valueKind": "Bool",
  "value": 42
}

### Malformed MAC (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "BAD-1",
  "mac": "not-a-mac",
  "location": "FacilityA/Zone1",
  "category": "Environmental",
  "expectedIntervalMs": 1000
}

### Duplicate MAC on a different node (expect 409)
POST {{host}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "BAD-2",
  "mac": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01",
  "location": "FacilityA/Zone1",
  "category": "Environmental",
  "expectedIntervalMs": 1000
}

### Batch with 2 good and 1 unregistered (expect 202, accepted 2 rejected 1)
POST {{host}}/api/telemetry/batch
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "nodeId": "METER-TEST", "timestampUtc": "2026-09-13T14:23:00Z", "category": "PowerConsumption", "valueKind": "Int", "value": 610 },
  { "nodeId": "GHOST",      "timestampUtc": "2026-09-13T14:23:00Z", "category": "PowerConsumption", "valueKind": "Int", "value": 999 },
  { "nodeId": "METER-TEST", "timestampUtc": "2026-09-13T14:23:01Z", "category": "PowerConsumption", "valueKind": "Int", "value": 625 }
]

###
### Part 2, real-time command stream
###

### 10. Register a soil sensor, a pump and a valve in the same sub-zone as the meter
POST {{host}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "SOIL-TEST",
  "mac": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02",
  "location": "FacilityA/Zone1/SubZoneB",
  "category": "Environmental",
  "expectedIntervalMs": 60000
}

###
POST {{host}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "PUMP-TEST",
  "mac": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:03",
  "location": "FacilityA/Zone1/SubZoneB",
  "category": "Actuator",
  "expectedIntervalMs": 60000
}

###
POST {{host}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "VALVE-TEST",
  "mac": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:04",
  "location": "FacilityA/Zone1/SubZoneB",
  "category": "Actuator",
  "expectedIntervalMs": 60000
}

### 11. The pump and valve report their state like a device would (pump off, valve open)
POST {{host}}/api/telemetry/batch
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "nodeId": "PUMP-TEST", "timestampUtc": "2026-10-17T10:00:00Z", "category": "Actuator", "valueKind": "Bool", "value": false },
  { "nodeId": "VALVE-TEST", "timestampUtc": "2026-10-17T10:00:00Z", "category": "Actuator", "valueKind": "Bool", "value": true }
]

### 12. Critically dry soil, this skips the FIFO queue and goes through the priority queue
POST {{host}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "SOIL-TEST",
  "timestampUtc": "2026-10-17T10:00:05Z",
  "category": "Environmental",
  "valueKind": "Float",
  "value": 12.5
}

### 13. Send it again, the hash set blocks the duplicate alert (suppressedDuplicates goes up)
POST {{host}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "SOIL-TEST",
  "timestampUtc": "2026-10-17T10:00:08Z",
  "category": "Environmental",
  "valueKind": "Float",
  "value": 11.9
}

### 14. Queue depth, throughput and how many alerts jumped the queue
GET {{host}}/api/stream/stats

### 15. Recent alerts, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/stream/alerts?limit=20

### 16. Disconnected nodes and active errors from the hash sets
GET {{host}}/api/stream/faults

### 17. Timestamp ordered readings for one device (sorted dictionary)
GET {{host}}/api/stream/timeline/SOIL-TEST?limit=100

### 18. Same thing limited to a time range
GET {{host}}/api/stream/timeline/SOIL-TEST?from=2026-10-17T10:00:00Z&to=2026-10-17T10:00:06Z

### 19. History feed of alerts, commands and dropouts
GET {{host}}/api/stream/events?limit=20

### 20. Live device table (dictionary keyed by node id)
GET {{host}}/api/devices

### 21. Filter by category and alert state
GET {{host}}/api/devices?category=Environmental&alertState=Alert

### 22. Search by node id or location level
GET {{host}}/api/devices?search=SubZoneB

### 23. Suggested actions, should include Start PUMP-TEST because the soil is dry and the pump is off
GET {{host}}/api/insights

### 24. Apply it, start the pump (expect 202, the device applies it when it checks in)
POST {{host}}/api/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "PUMP-TEST",
  "type": "StartPump"
}

### 25. Shut every valve in one command
POST {{host}}/api/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "ShutAllValves"
}

### 26. The undo stack, nextUndo is the shut all
GET {{host}}/api/commands/history

### 27. What the pump picks up when it checks in, a second call comes back empty
GET {{host}}/api/commands/pending/PUMP-TEST

### 28. Undo the shut all, every valve goes back to how it was
POST {{host}}/api/commands/undo

### 29. Undo the pump start
POST {{host}}/api/commands/undo

### 30. Nothing left (expect 409)
POST {{host}}/api/commands/undo

### 31. Tell the engine the operator looked at a device, this is what it learns from
POST {{host}}/api/insights/activity
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "View",
  "term": "PUMP-TEST"
}

### 32. Hide a suggestion for 10 minutes
POST {{host}}/api/insights/act-startpump-pump-test/dismiss

### 33. What the engine has learned so far
GET {{host}}/api/insights/patterns

###
### Part 2 rejection cases
###

### Pump command sent to a valve (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/api/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "VALVE-TEST",
  "type": "StartPump"
}

### Command sent to a sensor (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/api/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nodeId": "SOIL-TEST",
  "type": "OpenValve"
}

### Range where from is after to (expect 400)
GET {{host}}/api/stream/timeline/SOIL-TEST?from=2026-10-17T11:00:00Z&to=2026-10-17T10:00:00Z

### Activity kind the dashboard isn't allowed to send (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/api/insights/activity
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "Command",
  "term": "PUMP-TEST"
}

### Clean up
DELETE {{host}}/api/sensors/METER-TEST

###
DELETE {{host}}/api/sensors/SOIL-TEST

###
DELETE {{host}}/api/sensors/PUMP-TEST

###
DELETE {{host}}/api/sensors/VALVE-TEST

### OpenAPI document
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
